<figure class="locality" data-r48-locality aria-labelledby="r48-title">
<figcaption id="r48-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Choose where access should be efficient</figcaption>
<div class="controls"><label>Table policy <select data-policy><option value="table">REGIONAL BY TABLE · eu-north</option><option value="row">REGIONAL BY ROW · each shop’s home</option><option value="global">GLOBAL · reference reads everywhere</option></select></label><label>Operation <select data-operation><option value="read">Current point read</option><option value="write">Update</option></select></label></div>
<div class="regions"><div><p class="panel-title">eu-north</p><p data-north>Home for both shops’ rows</p></div><div><p class="panel-title">eu-west</p><p data-west>Requests reach eu-north</p></div><div><p class="panel-title">us-east</p><p data-us>Requests reach eu-north</p></div></div>
<p class="contract" data-contract aria-live="polite">The whole table has one home. A request from another region still reaches that home for an ordinary current read.</p>
<p class="caption">A comparison of access contracts, not a replica map or measured route. Shop 10’s home is eu-north; shop 20’s is eu-west. Regional-by-table deliberately gives this entire example table one home. GLOBAL describes suitable reference data, not a recommendation for frequently updated stock. Other replicas exist; the database survival goal separately governs voting placement. Eligible historical reads are outside this comparison.</p>
</figure>
<script>
const root=document.querySelector('[data-r48-locality]');if(root){const policy=root.querySelector('[data-policy]') as HTMLSelectElement,operation=root.querySelector('[data-operation]') as HTMLSelectElement;const draw=()=>{const p=policy.value,w=operation.value==='write';const v=p==='table'?['Home for both shops’ rows','Requests reach eu-north','Requests reach eu-north',w?'One table home coordinates updates. With region survival, the range still needs agreement outside its home.':'The whole table has one home. A request from another region still reaches that home for an ordinary current read.']:p==='row'?['Home for shop 10’s rows','Home for shop 20’s rows','Requests reach the selected row’s home',w?'Each shop’s updates go to its row home. A transaction touching different homes or a shared rule still crosses that boundary; region-surviving replication also needs a remote vote.':'Each shop can read its own rows from its home region. A query without a known region may search more partitions; locality does not identify the tenant for you.']:w?['Write coordination','Replicated reference data','Replicated reference data','GLOBAL pays additional coordination and timestamp-related write cost to support current reads across regions. It does not create an independent writable copy in every region.']:['Current reference reads','Current reference reads','Current reference reads','GLOBAL is intended to support low-latency current reads across all database regions. This is distinct from choosing an old AS OF SYSTEM TIME snapshot.'];['north','west','us','contract'].forEach((k,i)=>root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`).textContent=v[i]);};policy.addEventListener('change',draw);operation.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();}
</script>
<style>
.locality{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.5rem}.controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2fr 1fr;gap:.7rem;padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);min-width:0}select{min-width:0;max-width:100%;font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.5rem}.regions{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.7rem;margin-top:1rem}.regions>div{border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.8rem}.regions p{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin:.6rem 0 0}.regions .panel-title{font-weight:600;margin:0}.contract{border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.7rem 1rem;font:.9rem/1.6 var(--font-sans)}.caption{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:550px){.controls,.regions{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
